  "definition": "Contact bond adhesive",
  "effectiveDate": "2019-10-17",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-A 1202.40",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1202.40 Contact bond adhesive",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1202.40 “Contact bond adhesive” means an adhesive that is designed for application to both surfaces to be bonded together, is allowed to dry before the two surfaces are placed in contact with each other, forms an immediate bond that is impossible, or difficult, to reposition after both adhesive-coated surfaces are placed in contact with each other, and does not need sustained pressure or clamping of surfaces after the adhesive-coated surfaces have been brought together using sufficient momentary pressure to establish full contact between both surfaces. The term does not include rubber cements that are primarily intended for use on paper substrates or vulcanized fluids that are designed and labeled for tire repair only.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html"
